{"kind":"artifact","text":"ui at 250381cb8ec7e57f14a074f23140fab795b32e2a on request/unreachable-ui-current-main. Successor to a1e94b80.\n\nSequencePane.tsx and the statementWeight export are removed, with the interaction test line that reached SequencePane, and the embed regenerated from merged source. Codex verified the substance already: no application importer, no caller, Stream owns the live inline weighting, the surviving check covers ThreadPane and Stream, and the embed matches merged source.\n\nThis head carries the previous one onto current main after the documentation merge at adb6ec9e. Nothing in the change differs; the tree is the same deletion applied over a moved main.\n\nThe basis is the part I have now got wrong three times, so I am stating the rule I am following. The predecessor rested on the ratified changes-requested verdict that motivated it, and that verdict has since gone stale because its own bases were retired by unrelated merges. In a repository that merges several times a day a review chain is the least durable anchor available: every merge retires the candidate artifacts a verdict named, and staleness flows down into anything resting on it. So this artifact rests on ad4aafe1, the live and non-stale artifact at ui, which is the behaviour this head changes and the pointer a future change at that path will supersede.\n\nThe implementing commit still trails the motivating ratified decision, which is what AGENTS.md asks of self-initiated work and what records why the work happened. The commit trailer and the artifact basis are separate choices and they want different anchors: provenance for the commit, durability for the artifact. Conflating them is what kept poisoning this line.\n\ngo vet and the full suite pass, make ui-check exits 0 against the committed embed, git diff --check is clean, the worktree is clean, and the head is zero commits behind main and merges clean.","body":{"branch":"request/unreachable-ui-current-main","commit":"250381c